          h2 FAQ and interactive help
          text Answers to common problems can be found at .
          link "frequently asked questions" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:FAQ
          text Or check out .
          link "where to ask questions or make comments" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Questions
          text New users should seek help at the  if they're having problems while editing Wikipedia.
          link Teahouse https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Teahouse
          text More complex questions can be posed at the . Volunteers will respond as soon as they're able.
          link "Help desk" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Help_desk
          text Or  and a volunteer will visit you there!
          link "ask for help on your talk page" https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Special:MyTalk&action=edit&section=new&preload=Help:Contents/helpmepreload&preloadtitle=Help+me%21
          text You can get live help with editing in the .
          link "help chatroom" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:IRC_help_disclaimer
          text For help with technical issues, ask at the .
          link "Village pump" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Village_pump_(technical)
        col
          h2 Factual questions
          text If  has not answered your question (), try the . Volunteers there will attempt to answer your questions on any topic, or point you toward the information you need.
          link "searching Wikipedia" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search
          text "for example, questions like \"Which country has the world's largest fishing fleet?\""
          link "Reference Desk" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Reference_desk
        col
          h2 Tip of the day
          text Linking articles: the internal link
          text (AKA Wikilinks) are a great way to alert users to pertinent information. However, remember that  can detract from an article. Only create links that are relevant to the context of the article.
          link "Internal links" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Linking
          link "excessive linking" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Linking#Overlinking_and_underlinking
          text Internal links are created by placing double  around the word you wish to link; for example: . You can  by adding the # sign and the name of the section after the article name. For example: .
          link brackets https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracket
          text [[Subject X]]
          link "link to a specific section" https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Section#Section_linking
          text [[Subject X#The beginning]]
